## 9. Consulting and Training Clarification

You may use the Materials internally to improve your own work.

You may not use the Materials as client-facing deliverables, paid workshop content, consulting assets, training materials, certification content, or commercial enablement materials without written permission from Productside.

For example:

Allowed:

* A Product Manager uses a Productside skill to improve a roadmap discussion.
* A product team uses a Productside worksheet in an internal planning session.
* A company uses the Materials internally to improve discovery, strategy, or AI workflows.

Not allowed without written permission:

* A consultant uses Productside plays as part of a paid client engagement.
* A training company includes Productside templates in a paid course.
* A SaaS company embeds Productside skills into a commercial AI assistant.
* A marketplace seller packages Productside prompts as a paid library.
* A firm rebrands Productside materials as its own methodology.

